n during primary percutaneous coronary intervention.</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><volume>358</volume><fpage>557</fpage><lpage>567</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18256391</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests: </bold>The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding: </bold>The authors have no support or funding to report.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>